{"tool_name":"gemma_algorithm","contents":["bioconda","bioschemas","biotools","debian","galaxy","oeb"],"identifiers":["biotools:gemma_algorithm","bioconda:gemma","galaxy:gemma","debian:gemma"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"gemma_algorithm","home":"http://www.xzlab.org/software.html","license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"Test for association in genome-wide association studies (GWAS) using a standard linear mixed model to account for population stratification and sample structure. It calculates exact Wald or likelihood ratio test statistics and p-values, and is computationally efficient for large GWAS.","addition_date":"2017-08-03T18:44:07Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-25T14:23:14.907115Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"collections":["Animal and Crop Genomics"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:gemma_algorithm","credit":[{"typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"],"url":"http://www.xzlab.org/contact.html"}],"documentation":[{"type":["User manual"],"url":"http://www.xzlab.org/software/GEMMAmanual.pdf"}],"edit_permission":{"authors":["animalandcropgenomics"],"type":"group"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Nucleic acid sequence analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2478"}]}],"name":"GEMMA","operating_system":["Linux","Mac"],"owner":"mbs_import","publication":[{"doi":"10.1038/ng.2310","metadata":{"abstract":"Linear mixed models have attracted considerable attention recently as a powerful and effective tool for accounting for population stratification and relatedness in genetic association tests. However, existing methods for exact computation of standard test statistics are computationally impractical for even moderate-sized genome-wide association studies. To address this issue, several approximate methods have been proposed. Here, we present an efficient exact method, which we refer to as genome-wide efficient mixed-model association (GEMMA), that makes approximations unnecessary in many contexts. This method is approximately n times faster than 